<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Teres I</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">5th century BCE</span> · <a href="/centuries/5th-century-bce">5th century BCE</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Teres I was the founder of the Odrysian kingdom of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/thrace">Thrace</a> in the 5th century BCE. After the Persian withdrawal from <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/europe">Europe</a> following 479 BCE he united Thracian tribes of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/maritsa">Hebrus</a> valley under Odrysian rule, and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/thucydides">Thucydides</a> names him as the first to make the kingdom great. His son <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/sitalces">Sitalces</a> extended Odrysian power from the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/aegean">Aegean</a> to the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/danube">Danube</a>.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/teres-i.jpg" alt="Teres I" width="320" height="245" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: ChernorizetsHrabar · CC BY-SA 4.0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:The_golden_life-size_mask_of_Teres_I_found_in_his_tomb_in_the_Valley_of_the_Thracian_Kings.png" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
